{#
    The report builder, as a PARTIAL.

    ⚠️ A partial and not a page, deliberately. A page carries a layout, a title, a menu entry, a
    permission check and a breadcrumb — every one of which belongs to the application. What the
    bundle can own is the body: four steps, their targets, and the wiring to the controller.

    Include it from your own page:

        include('@Dataflow/report/_builder.html.twig', {
            entities:   report_entities,
            fields_url: path('app_report_builder_fields'),
            run_url:    path('app_report_builder_run'),
            export_url: path('app_report_builder_export'),
            save_url:   path('app_report_builder_save'),
            load_url:   path('app_report_builder_load', {id: '__ID__'})|replace({__ID__: '{id}'}),
            can_share:  is_granted('report:builder:share'),
        })

    `entities` is a map of FQCN to a hash carrying a `label`.

    ⚠️ **Twig comments do not nest**, which is why the line above is prose and why this block
    contains no comment delimiter of its own. Written the obvious way — a nested comment annotating
    the `entities` line — this block closed at the INNER terminator, and everything after it
    (thirteen lines of prose plus five path calls) was printed onto the page, above the stepper.
    `lint:twig` passes either way: the file is valid Twig, just not the Twig anybody meant. Only
    opening the screen showed it, and I made the mistake twice — the second time inside the warning
    about the first.

    ⚠️ `load_url` must contain the literal `{id}`. Generating it with a placeholder and swapping it
    back is the readable way to get one out of a router that insists on a real value — the version
    this replaces generated `id: 0` and had the CONTROLLER patch the URL with a regular expression.

    ⚠️ `can_share` is a boolean the application computes. The bundle must not call `is_granted()`
    with a permission code it invented: the codes are the project's, and a bundle guessing one gets
    "false" everywhere, which hides the control on every screen and looks like a broken feature.
#}
{% set stimulus = stimulus|default(dataflow_stimulus|default('dataflow--report-builder')) %}
{% set entities = entities|default({}) %}
{% set can_share = can_share|default(false) %}
{% set steps = [
    {key: 'entity',  target: 'stepEntity',  label: 'dataflow.builder.step.entity',  icon: 'fa-cube'},
    {key: 'columns', target: 'stepColumns', label: 'dataflow.builder.step.columns', icon: 'fa-list-check'},
    {key: 'filters', target: 'stepFilters', label: 'dataflow.builder.step.filters', icon: 'fa-filter'},
    {key: 'export',  target: 'stepExport',  label: 'dataflow.builder.step.export',  icon: 'fa-magnifying-glass-chart'}
] %}

<div data-controller="{{ stimulus }}"
     data-{{ stimulus }}-fields-url-value="{{ fields_url|default('') }}"
     data-{{ stimulus }}-run-url-value="{{ run_url|default('') }}"
     data-{{ stimulus }}-export-url-value="{{ export_url|default('') }}"
     data-{{ stimulus }}-save-url-value="{{ save_url|default('') }}"
     data-{{ stimulus }}-load-url-value="{{ load_url|default('') }}"
     class="space-y-6">

    {# The stepper. `.step-tab` and its bullet are styled by assets/styles/dataflow.css; the
       controller only toggles `.is-current` / `.is-done`. #}
    <div class="form-panel !py-3">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1 overflow-x-auto" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="stepTabs">
            {% for i, step in steps %}
                <button type="button" class="step-tab" data-step="{{ step.key }}" data-step-index="{{ i }}"
                        data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#gotoStep">
                    <span class="step-tab-bullet">{{ i + 1 }}</span>
                    <i class="fa-solid {{ step.icon }}"></i>
                    <span class="font-medium">{{ step.label|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</span>
                </button>
                {% if not loop.last %}
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-slate-300 dark:text-slate-600 text-xs"></i>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Step 1 — the root entity #}
    <div class="form-panel step-panel" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="stepEntity">
        <h2 class="form-section-title">{{ 'dataflow.builder.entity.heading'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">{{ 'dataflow.builder.entity.help'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            {% for fqcn, meta in entities %}
                <label class="flex items-center gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-50 dark:hover:bg-slate-800/50">
                    <input type="radio" name="entity" value="{{ fqcn }}"
                           data-action="change->{{ stimulus }}#entityChanged"
                           data-{{ stimulus }}-target="entityRadio">
                    <span class="text-sm font-medium">{{ meta.label|default(fqcn) }}</span>
                </label>
            {% else %}
                {# ⚠️ Not an error state. An empty catalogue is what an application that has
                   registered no ReportableEntityProviderInterface legitimately shows. #}
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 col-span-3">{{ 'dataflow.builder.entity.empty'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Step 2 — columns: available on the left, the ordered selection on the right #}
    <div class="form-panel step-panel" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="stepColumns" hidden>
        <h2 class="form-section-title">{{ 'dataflow.builder.columns.heading'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">{{ 'dataflow.builder.columns.help'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <div class="lg:col-span-2">
                <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500 mb-2">{{ 'dataflow.builder.columns.available'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</h3>
                <div data-{{ stimulus }}-target="columnsList" class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 max-h-[60vh] overflow-y-auto pr-1"></div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500 mb-2">{{ 'dataflow.builder.columns.selected'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</h3>
                <div data-{{ stimulus }}-target="selectedColumnsList" class="space-y-1 max-h-[60vh] overflow-y-auto pr-1"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Step 3 — filters #}
    <div class="form-panel step-panel" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="stepFilters" hidden>
        <h2 class="form-section-title">{{ 'dataflow.builder.filters.heading'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">{{ 'dataflow.builder.filters.help'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
        <div data-{{ stimulus }}-target="filtersList" class="space-y-2"></div>
        <button type="button" class="btn-secondary mt-3 text-xs" data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#addFilter">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> {{ 'dataflow.builder.filters.add'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}
        </button>
    </div>

    {# Step 4 — preview, export, save #}
    <div class="form-panel step-panel" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="stepExport" hidden>
        <h2 class="form-section-title">{{ 'dataflow.builder.export.heading'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</h2>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
            <fieldset class="form-fieldset !mb-0">
                <legend class="text-xs">{{ 'dataflow.builder.export.preview'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</legend>
                <button type="button" class="btn-primary w-full" data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#preview">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> {{ 'dataflow.builder.export.preview_run'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}
                </button>
            </fieldset>

            <fieldset class="form-fieldset !mb-0">
                <legend class="text-xs">{{ 'dataflow.builder.export.section_export'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</legend>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2">
                    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary text-xs" data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#exportCsv">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-csv"></i> CSV
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary text-xs" data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#exportXlsx">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-excel"></i> XLSX
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary text-xs" data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#exportJson">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> JSON
                    </button>
                </div>
            </fieldset>

            <fieldset class="form-fieldset !mb-0">
                <legend class="text-xs">{{ 'dataflow.builder.export.section_save'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</legend>
                <div class="flex gap-2">
                    <input type="text" placeholder="{{ 'dataflow.builder.export.name_placeholder'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}"
                           data-{{ stimulus }}-target="reportName" class="form-control text-sm flex-1">
                    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary text-xs whitespace-nowrap" data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#save">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i>
                    </button>
                </div>
                {# ⚠️ Hidden without the permission, AND refused by the server. Hiding alone is not a
                   guard — the payload carries `shareScope` and anyone can set it — but showing a
                   control the server will downgrade is its own defect. #}
                {% if can_share %}
                    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer">
                        <input type="checkbox" class="rounded"
                               data-{{ stimulus }}-target="shareToggle"
                               data-action="change->{{ stimulus }}#toggleShare">
                        <span>{{ 'dataflow.builder.export.share_scope_organization'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}</span>
                    </label>
                {% endif %}
            </fieldset>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 rounded-lg"
             data-{{ stimulus }}-target="previewPanel" hidden>
            <table class="min-w-full text-xs">
                <thead class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800">
                    <tr data-{{ stimulus }}-target="previewHeader"></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-{{ stimulus }}-target="previewBody" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800"></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Previous / next #}
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-2">
        <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="prevBtn"
                data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#prevStep">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left"></i> {{ 'dataflow.builder.step.prev'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}
        </button>
        <span class="text-xs text-slate-400" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="stepIndicator"></span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-primary" data-{{ stimulus }}-target="nextBtn"
                data-action="click->{{ stimulus }}#nextStep">
            {{ 'dataflow.builder.step.next'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }} <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right"></i>
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
